## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates understanding of edge cryptography implementation, privacy-preserving design, and business impact analysis in payment systems—skills critical for roles at Cloudflare, Square, and similar fintech companies.

## Key Concepts
- On-device cryptographic verification using Ed25519 and platform crypto APIs
- Key management lifecycle and rotation strategies
- Mobile device constraints: latency, CPU, memory, and energy budgets
- Local telemetry architecture and storage growth patterns
- Regulatory compliance frameworks for payment verification
- Financial modeling with go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify an Ed25519 signature on-device
async function verifyReceipt(receipt, publicKey) {
  // receipt: { data: ArrayBuffer, signature: ArrayBuffer }
  const isValid = await crypto.subtle.verify(
    'Ed25519',
    publicKey,
    receipt.signature,
    receipt.data
  );
  return isValid;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This probes a candidate's ability to quantify costs for an on-device feature with privacy constraints and optional cloud lifts, focusing on edge-cases and governance.

## Key Concepts
- On-device storage budgeting
- Edge compute energy budget
- Privacy/compliance & consent overhead
- Rollout strategy and drift maintenance

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost(storageMB, cpuW, users, cloudPerUser) {
  const storageCost = storageMB * 0.01;
  const energyCost = cpuW * 24 * 365 * 0.0003;
  const telemetry = users * cloudPerUser;
  return storageCost + energyCost + telemetry;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the break-even horizon with real usage data?
- What safeguards would you implement for data minimization and consent revocation?

